    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d359">

                <pb facs="0329" n="317" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg317"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.5245/46</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Governor of
                        California</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Warren</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-09">August 9, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Governor Warren</hi>: I have received your
                    letter of July 8, 1943, in which you inform me that your signature has been
                    affixed to Senate Bill No. 140, and in which you discuss certain aspects of the
                    bill.</p>
                <p>I am grateful to you for the explanation of the basis and purpose of this bill,
                    as set forth in your several communications on the subject. The Department will
                    convey to those persons who have communicated on the matter with it, the
                    substance of your remarks. Your portrayal of the subject will, I am confident,
                    be most helpful in alleviating such bitterness and resentment as may exist
                    regarding the bill’s passage.</p>
                <p>With my appreciation of your expression of good wishes, I am</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cordell Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
